WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:06.012
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online Newspaper Class, level two.

2
00:00:06.312 --> 00:00:09.501
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.801 --> 00:00:16.633
Unit nine: E-commerce Trends. Today you will express concession with despite, in spite of and even though.

4
00:00:16.933 --> 00:00:19.458
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.552
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:24.417 --> 00:00:26.010
Online marketplace.

7
00:00:27.017 --> 00:00:31.222
Online marketplace means a website where many sellers offer goods to buyers.

8
00:00:31.817 --> 00:00:35.465
Small sellers reach customers on an online marketplace.

9
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.004
Your turn. Say: Online marketplace.

10
00:00:41.867 --> 00:00:43.402
Online marketplace.

11
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.499
Checkout process.

12
00:00:46.483 --> 00:00:50.828
Checkout process means the steps a customer follows to pay for an online order.

13
00:00:51.417 --> 00:00:54.148
A simple checkout process increases sales.

14
00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.890
Your turn. Say: Checkout process.

15
00:01:00.733 --> 00:01:02.141
Checkout process.

16
00:01:02.883 --> 00:01:03.942
Digital payment.

17
00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:08.645
Digital payment means paying for goods using electronic methods.

18
00:01:09.250 --> 00:01:11.528
Digital payment is fast and convenient.

19
00:01:12.117 --> 00:01:15.094
Your turn. Say: Digital payment.

20
00:01:17.933 --> 00:01:19.039
Digital payment.

21
00:01:19.783 --> 00:01:21.295
Shipping logistics.

22
00:01:22.283 --> 00:01:26.442
Shipping logistics means the organisation of delivering goods to customers.

23
00:01:27.050 --> 00:01:30.396
Shipping logistics decide how quickly parcels arrive.

24
00:01:30.983 --> 00:01:34.367
Your turn. Say: Shipping logistics.

25
00:01:37.233 --> 00:01:38.815
Shipping logistics.

26
00:01:39.550 --> 00:01:40.795
Customer review.

27
00:01:41.783 --> 00:01:45.223
Customer review means an opinion written by a buyer about a product.

28
00:01:45.817 --> 00:01:48.315
A good customer review builds trust.

29
00:01:48.917 --> 00:01:51.848
Your turn. Say: Customer review.

30
00:01:54.700 --> 00:01:56.282
Customer review.

31
00:01:57.017 --> 00:01:58.296
Mobile shopping.

32
00:01:59.283 --> 00:02:02.339
Mobile shopping means buying goods using a smartphone.

33
00:02:02.950 --> 00:02:04.984
Mobile shopping grows every year.

34
00:02:05.583 --> 00:02:08.526
Your turn. Say: Mobile shopping.

35
00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:12.565
Mobile shopping.

36
00:02:13.317 --> 00:02:14.654
Conversion rate.

37
00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:19.565
Conversion rate means the percentage of visitors who actually buy something.

38
00:02:20.150 --> 00:02:22.405
A better photo raised the conversion rate.

39
00:02:23.017 --> 00:02:25.518
Your turn. Say: Conversion rate.

40
00:02:28.367 --> 00:02:29.623
Conversion rate.

41
00:02:30.383 --> 00:02:31.477
Cart abandonment.

42
00:02:32.483 --> 00:02:36.340
Cart abandonment means when a shopper leaves without completing a purchase.

43
00:02:36.950 --> 00:02:39.170
Hidden fees cause cart abandonment.

44
00:02:39.783 --> 00:02:42.215
Your turn. Say: Cart abandonment.

45
00:02:45.067 --> 00:02:46.370
Cart abandonment.

46
00:02:47.167 --> 00:02:51.166
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:52.017 --> 00:02:59.278
Visal, an article says 'Despite rapid growth, online shops still lose many customers at checkout.' What does 'despite' mean?

48
00:03:00.383 --> 00:03:11.903
It shows contrast, like although, but it is followed by a noun or -ing: despite rapid growth, despite having low prices.

49
00:03:13.017 --> 00:03:13.971
And 'even though'?

50
00:03:15.083 --> 00:03:24.295
Even though is followed by a clause and is stronger: 'Even though the shipping was free, many shoppers abandoned their carts.'

51
00:03:25.383 --> 00:03:26.860
Why do shoppers leave?

52
00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:36.799
In spite of attractive prices, a slow checkout process or unexpected fees can reduce the conversion rate.

53
00:03:37.933 --> 00:03:39.422
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:40.283 --> 00:03:44.384
Grammar focus: Concession: despite and in spite of and even though.

55
00:03:44.684 --> 00:03:45.964
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:46.650 --> 00:03:50.542
Despite rapid growth, many shops lose customers at checkout.

57
00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:55.191
Even though shipping was free, many shoppers left their carts.

58
00:03:56.083 --> 00:03:59.824
In spite of having low prices, the site had a low conversion rate.

59
00:04:00.767 --> 00:04:09.041
Despite / in spite of + noun or -ing (never 'despite of'). Even though / although + subject + verb. All three show a surprising contrast.

60
00:04:09.783 --> 00:04:14.084
Be careful! Don't say: Despite of the price, we bought it.

61
00:04:16.033 --> 00:04:19.078
Say: Despite the price, we bought it.

62
00:04:19.378 --> 00:04:21.412
Say 'despite', not 'despite of'.

63
00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:24.887
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:27.467
Why Carts Are Left Behind.

65
00:04:27.767 --> 00:04:32.135
Online shopping has grown quickly, and mobile shopping now leads the trend.

66
00:04:33.133 --> 00:04:37.606
Despite this growth, cart abandonment remains high on every online marketplace.

67
00:04:38.600 --> 00:04:43.711
Even though a digital payment takes seconds, a long checkout process can drive buyers away.

68
00:04:44.700 --> 00:04:50.577
In spite of good prices, poor shipping logistics and weak customer reviews also reduce the conversion rate.

69
00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:55.470
Successful shops therefore make buying simple, clear and trustworthy.

70
00:04:56.567 --> 00:05:00.510
Part five: quiz. Five questions. Are you ready?

71
00:05:01.350 --> 00:05:04.778
blank rapid growth, many shops lose customers.

72
00:05:05.078 --> 00:05:09.044
A, Despite. B, Even though. C, Despite of.

73
00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:14.669
The answer is A: Despite.

74
00:05:15.817 --> 00:05:18.908
blank shipping was free, shoppers left their carts.

75
00:05:19.208 --> 00:05:23.093
A, Even though. B, Despite. C, Because of.

76
00:05:26.633 --> 00:05:28.528
The answer is A: Even though.

77
00:05:29.683 --> 00:05:32.914
The percentage of visitors who actually buy is the blank rate.

78
00:05:33.214 --> 00:05:36.739
A, conversion. B, shipping. C, review.

79
00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:42.218
The answer is A: conversion.

80
00:05:43.383 --> 00:05:45.081
Choose the correct sentence.

81
00:05:45.381 --> 00:05:52.297
A, Despite of the price, we bought it.. B, Despite the price, we bought it.. C, Despite the price was low, we bought it..

82
00:05:55.833 --> 00:05:58.947
The answer is B: Despite the price, we bought it..

83
00:06:00.083 --> 00:06:02.896
According to the reading, successful shops make buying…

84
00:06:03.196 --> 00:06:08.556
A, simple, clear and trustworthy. B, slow and secret. C, expensive.

85
00:06:12.100 --> 00:06:15.481
The answer is A: simple, clear and trustworthy.

86
00:06:16.667 --> 00:06:20.050
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

87
00:06:20.917 --> 00:06:25.319
Why might a customer abandon their shopping cart before completing an online purchase?

88
00:06:34.117 --> 00:06:35.698
Now listen to Visal.

89
00:06:35.998 --> 00:06:58.509
A customer might abandon a cart because of unexpected costs such as shipping or taxes, which appear only at the end. Others leave when the checkout process is long, or when they do not trust the payment security. Some are only comparing prices, even though they like the product. Clear information and a simple checkout can reduce this problem.

90
00:06:58.809 --> 00:07:00.483
Excellent answer, Visal!

91
00:07:01.383 --> 00:07:08.134
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and concession: despite and in spite of and even though.

92
00:07:08.434 --> 00:07:12.944
Today's value is digital trust. Protect the trust that others place in you.

93
00:07:13.244 --> 00:07:15.687
See you in Unit ten. Goodbye!

94
00:07:15.987 --> 00:07:19.069
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

